current_canonical:
A1 #[op] macro expands methods on OpsRuntime into inventory-registered entries dispatched by CLI/MCP/REST adapters. Example:

```rust
#[op(cli = "recall", mcp = "rein_recall")]
pub fn recall(&self, query: &str) -> OpsResult<Vec<Memory>> {
    self.store.recall(query)
}
```

```rust
inventory::submit!(AuthPolicy::localhost_only("recall"));
```

evidence.content:
the dedup path uses BEGIN IMMEDIATE to prevent concurrent races:

```sql
BEGIN IMMEDIATE;
SELECT id FROM memories WHERE jaccard_sim(content, ?) > 0.70;
COMMIT;
```

current_canonical:
store_with_dedup uses BEGIN IMMEDIATE to prevent concurrent dedup races. The feedback_events table is append-only.

```sql
BEGIN IMMEDIATE;
SELECT id FROM memories WHERE jaccard_sim(content, ?) > 0.70;
COMMIT;
```

```sql
CREATE TABLE feedback_events (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  event_type TEXT NOT NULL,
  payload BLOB,
  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL
);
```

